<p>A common pitfall is submitting an RC with mismatched chassis or engine numbers; our team verifies these details against the chassis number plate to prevent rejection at the Pune RTO. We handle the entire application for the new Maharashtra RC, ensuring your vehicle is legally registered in your new state within the statutory time limit.</p><h3>e‑Way Bill and Transport Compliance</h3><p>For long-distance transport exceeding 50 kilometers, an e‑Way Bill is mandatory under GST regulations. This digital document must match the vehicle’s registration number, the transporter’s GSTIN, and the exact distance. Missing or incorrect e‑Way bills are a primary cause of detention at check posts.</p>
<p>Our logistics specialists generate and verify this bill in real-time, ensuring it aligns perfectly with the physical movement of your car. We also manage the Goods and Services Tax (GST) invoice, which serves as the supporting document for the e‑Way Bill, eliminating the risk of penalties for non-compliance.</p><h3>Insurance and Financial Proof</h3><p>Your current comprehensive insurance policy must be valid throughout the journey. However, standard policies often exclude damage during professional transport. We advise adding a specific transit cover or verifying the policy’s terms with your insurer.</p>
<p>We assist in obtaining a transit insurance certificate that explicitly covers the Delhi-to-Pune route, providing peace of mind against accidents or theft. Additionally, ensure your Finance Company, if applicable, has issued a lien release or NOC, as Pune authorities will not process the RC transfer without this financial clearance.</p><h3>State-Specific Clearances and Border Checkpoints</h3><p>Crossing state borders requires vigilance. While there are no specific "clearance permits" for private cars, police checkpoints may scrutinize your documents. Our drivers carry a complete, organized file containing the NOC, e‑Way Bill, insurance, and a copy of your ID.</p>
